Steps
Step 1: Set Up Log Ingestion with Logstash
Create a sample log file:
mkdir -p ~/elk-nlp-lab/logs
echo "[2025-07-09] ERROR: User login failed due to invalid credentials." >> ~/elk-nlp-lab/logs/system.log
echo "[2025-07-09] WARNING: Unusual login location detected." >> ~/elk-nlp-lab/logs/system.log
Create a Logstash config:
nano ~/elk-nlp-lab/logstash.conf
input {
  file {
    path => "/home/<your-username>/elk-nlp-lab/logs/system.log"
    start_position => "beginning"
    sincedb_path => "/dev/null"
  }
}
filter {
  grok {
    match => { "message" => "\[%{TIMESTAMP_ISO8601:timestamp}\] %{LOGLEVEL:level}: %{GREEDYDATA:msg}" }
  }
}
output {
  elasticsearch {
    hosts => ["http://localhost:9200"]
    index => "compliance-logs"
  }
  stdout { codec => rubydebug }
}
Replace <your-username> with your actual Ubuntu user.

Run Logstash:
sudo /usr/share/logstash/bin/logstash -f ~/elk-nlp-lab/logstash.conf
